WEBVTT

00:00:00.602 --> 00:00:01.390
Hello everyone.

00:00:01.629 --> 00:00:03.390
Today we talk about infills.

00:00:03.818 --> 00:00:08.270
Clients who have builder gel or acrylic come back a few weeks later for an infill.

00:00:08.613 --> 00:00:13.230
Done right, the set lasts a very long time, always balanced and strong.

00:00:13.657 --> 00:00:16.951
Done wrong, or left too long, the nails break and lift,

00:00:16.901 --> 00:00:19.310
and the client thinks it is the product.

00:00:19.919 --> 00:00:23.073
First, let us look at what happens as the nail grows.

00:00:23.679 --> 00:00:26.265
The natural nail grows out a little every day,

00:00:26.215 --> 00:00:28.913
and it carries the gel or acrylic layer with it.

00:00:29.479 --> 00:00:34.113
At the cuticle, a strip of new natural nail appears, with nothing covering it.

00:00:34.699 --> 00:00:36.753
That strip gets wider week by week.

00:00:37.268 --> 00:00:40.113
Where the old layer stops, there is a small step.

00:00:40.702 --> 00:00:42.912
But what matters more is the apex.

00:00:43.224 --> 00:00:47.063
On the day of the service, the apex sits right over the stress area,

00:00:47.013 --> 00:00:48.512
slightly towards the back.

00:00:48.947 --> 00:00:52.832
As the nail grows, the apex slowly moves towards the tip too.

00:00:53.250 --> 00:00:55.232
The thickest part now sits in front.

00:00:55.645 --> 00:00:57.952
The nail gets longer, and top heavy.

00:00:58.551 --> 00:00:59.559
Picture a lever.

00:00:59.788 --> 00:01:01.686
The longer and heavier the tip,

00:01:01.636 --> 00:01:05.799
the more force goes into the stress area every time the client types,

00:01:05.829 --> 00:01:08.599
opens a lid, or knocks her hand against something.

00:01:08.937 --> 00:01:12.599
And right now, that area is no longer supported by the apex.

00:01:13.019 --> 00:01:16.640
The result is that the nail breaks straight across, right there,

00:01:16.590 --> 00:01:18.759
or the product pops up at the cuticle,

00:01:18.788 --> 00:01:19.959
and gradually lifts.

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:24.520
So do not wait until a nail breaks or lifts before doing an infill.

00:01:24.846 --> 00:01:28.280
With builder gel, it is usually every three to four weeks.

00:01:28.594 --> 00:01:31.480
With acrylic, usually every two to three weeks.

00:01:31.663 --> 00:01:33.240
That is only the usual range.

00:01:33.588 --> 00:01:36.689
It depends on how fast the nails of each person grow,

00:01:36.639 --> 00:01:38.760
what the client does with her hands,

00:01:38.869 --> 00:01:39.560
and the brand.

00:01:39.901 --> 00:01:44.200
Fast growing nails, or heavy work with the hands, mean booking sooner.

00:01:44.818 --> 00:01:47.968
When the appointment comes, the first question is always:

00:01:48.145 --> 00:01:50.688
infill, or remove it all and start again?

00:01:51.154 --> 00:01:54.085
Infill, when the old layer is still firmly bonded,

00:01:54.035 --> 00:01:57.888
with just a little lifting at the edge that filing will take away.

00:01:58.228 --> 00:02:01.757
Remove it all, when the old layer has lifted in large patches,

00:02:01.707 --> 00:02:03.328
with air pockets underneath.

00:02:03.495 --> 00:02:08.565
If you see a green mark or discoloration under the lifted part, if the nail hurts,

00:02:08.515 --> 00:02:09.728
is red and swollen,

00:02:10.056 --> 00:02:13.684
or the natural nail is separating from the bed, do nothing more,

00:02:13.634 --> 00:02:15.808
and advise the client to see a doctor.

00:02:16.343 --> 00:02:18.928
Review the lesson on when not to treat a client.

00:02:19.277 --> 00:02:22.528
And for removing it properly, there is the gel removal lesson.

00:02:23.177 --> 00:02:24.935
There is something that happens a lot:

00:02:25.188 --> 00:02:27.712
you see a little lifting, you are in a hurry,

00:02:27.662 --> 00:02:30.295
so you build gel or acrylic over it to seal it.

00:02:30.552 --> 00:02:31.495
It looks nice.

00:02:31.882 --> 00:02:36.455
But under that lifted part, water, oil and dirt have already got in.

00:02:36.963 --> 00:02:40.375
Building over it traps them inside, warm and damp.

00:02:40.857 --> 00:02:43.689
That is a place for bacteria and fungi to grow,

00:02:43.639 --> 00:02:46.055
and the natural nail underneath suffers.

00:02:46.301 --> 00:02:48.535
And the new layer will lift very quickly too.

00:02:48.962 --> 00:02:50.055
So the rule is:

00:02:50.188 --> 00:02:55.729
wherever it has lifted, file it all away, until the remaining edge is firmly bonded,

00:02:55.679 --> 00:02:56.055
thin,

00:02:56.162 --> 00:02:57.415
and flush with the nail.

00:02:57.955 --> 00:03:00.776
For infills, use the same type of product.

00:03:00.939 --> 00:03:02.216
Gel on gel.

00:03:02.344 --> 00:03:03.656
Acrylic on acrylic.

00:03:04.162 --> 00:03:07.485
If you want to use two different types, or two different brands,

00:03:07.435 --> 00:03:10.296
check whether the brand says they can be used together.

00:03:10.708 --> 00:03:12.456
Many brands make a whole system:

00:03:12.805 --> 00:03:16.216
the bonding layer, the gel and the top coat go together.

00:03:16.565 --> 00:03:19.504
Mix them at random, and sometimes they do not bond,

00:03:19.454 --> 00:03:21.656
and sometimes they do not cure evenly.

00:03:22.298 --> 00:03:25.262
An infill is not just filling the gap at the cuticle.

00:03:25.611 --> 00:03:28.222
The most important job is to rebalance the set.

00:03:28.809 --> 00:03:32.782
File the old layer thinner, especially the thick part that has moved forward.

00:03:33.291 --> 00:03:36.141
If the nails have grown too long, cut them shorter,

00:03:36.091 --> 00:03:38.062
keeping the shape the client chose.

00:03:38.491 --> 00:03:42.942
Then build over the new growth, and rebuild the apex back in its proper place:

00:03:43.291 --> 00:03:45.742
over the stress area, slightly towards the back.

00:03:45.975 --> 00:03:48.492
When the infill is done, seen from the side,

00:03:48.442 --> 00:03:51.182
the nail should look just like on the first day.

00:03:51.847 --> 00:03:53.427
Something else that happens a lot:

00:03:53.775 --> 00:03:56.707
many infills without filing the old layer thinner.

00:03:57.056 --> 00:03:58.867
Another layer added every time.

00:03:59.216 --> 00:04:02.917
The set gets thicker and thicker, stiff, heavy looking,

00:04:02.867 --> 00:04:05.507
and loses its natural shape completely.

00:04:05.934 --> 00:04:07.016
So at every infill,

00:04:06.966 --> 00:04:10.547
the old layer must be filed thinner before the new layer goes on.

00:04:10.804 --> 00:04:14.808
And when the old layer has lifted in many places, or is discolored,

00:04:14.758 --> 00:04:17.347
remove it all and start again from scratch.

00:04:17.602 --> 00:04:19.667
That is what is good for the nails of the client.

00:04:20.193 --> 00:04:24.068
When filing, there is one area where you must be extremely careful:

00:04:24.321 --> 00:04:25.268
the cuticle area.

00:04:25.697 --> 00:04:29.108
That is new natural nail, still thin and soft.

00:04:29.472 --> 00:04:32.308
Just glide a buffer very lightly to remove the shine.

00:04:32.772 --> 00:04:36.628
Do not file deep into the natural nail, and do not file the skin.

00:04:37.057 --> 00:04:41.744
File into the natural nail, and with every infill the nail gets a bit thinner,

00:04:41.694 --> 00:04:43.588
the client feels heat and pain,

00:04:43.777 --> 00:04:45.508
and the nail gradually weakens.

00:04:45.674 --> 00:04:50.148
File into the skin, and you create an open wound, a way in for bacteria.

00:04:50.487 --> 00:04:52.847
With a hand file or an electric file alike,

00:04:52.797 --> 00:04:55.588
always keep the tip of the file away from the skin.

00:04:56.216 --> 00:04:59.350
Infills mean a lot of filing, so a lot of dust.

00:04:59.683 --> 00:05:03.430
Switch on the extraction at the table, and wear a mask and gloves.

00:05:03.763 --> 00:05:04.950
Brush the dust away;

00:05:05.009 --> 00:05:05.910
do not blow.

00:05:06.171 --> 00:05:11.384
Dust from gel that is not fully cured, or gel on the skin, can both cause allergies,

00:05:11.334 --> 00:05:13.350
for the client and for yourself.

00:05:13.719 --> 00:05:17.270
For more detail, review the lesson on allergies and chemicals.

00:05:17.437 --> 00:05:21.110
Rules on products and dust extraction differ from country to country.

00:05:21.769 --> 00:05:23.998
Finally, be honest with the client.

00:05:24.326 --> 00:05:28.723
A set that gets its infills on time, and is rebalanced every time,

00:05:28.673 --> 00:05:30.238
lasts a very long time,

00:05:30.302 --> 00:05:32.078
and the natural nails stay healthy.

00:05:32.493 --> 00:05:37.598
A set left past its time becomes top heavy, and sooner or later it breaks or lifts.

00:05:37.998 --> 00:05:40.356
Then it often has to be removed completely,

00:05:40.306 --> 00:05:42.718
costing the client more time and more money.

00:05:43.046 --> 00:05:46.878
So book the next infill right before the client leaves, and explain why.

00:05:47.519 --> 00:05:50.800
You see, an infill is not just adding more product.

00:05:50.907 --> 00:05:52.320
It is reading the set again:

00:05:52.611 --> 00:05:57.440
where it has lifted, where the apex has drifted, and then rebalancing it properly.

00:05:57.867 --> 00:06:00.400
Once you understand it, your hands will follow.

00:06:00.734 --> 00:06:03.920
In the practice lesson, we will go step by step together.

00:06:04.171 --> 00:06:06.800
And now, take the short quiz below the video.

00:06:07.056 --> 00:06:07.920
See you next time.
